## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/env/io_execution_env.dart | ⚠️ important stop exit survivor adoption card b ships with no behavioral test at either call site the pr s user visible fix — a stopped timed out exit scans for survivors on hosts without group leadership and adoption re tracks them — is covered only by the pure shouldscansurvivors truth table and the killtree seam tests nothing asserts the call site behavior this gate exists for a stopped background job on a non owngroup host actually buffers survivors at exit io execution env dart 1330 1336 and the registry s settle listener adopts them shell jobs dart listensettle a timeout d cancelled foreground exec reports and adopts survivors io execution env dart 1032 1045 → adoptexecsurvivors a regression that flips the gate at a call site — e g passing owngroup true unconditionally or dropping the stopped argument — ships silently and the tool answers stopped again while the term trapping grandchild lives on the exact bug 2276 is about the truth table test would still pass — it pins the pure function not its callers ask one seam registry level test that a stopped non owngroup job s buffered survivors get adopted and one assertion that a timeout d non owngroup exec carries survivors in its result both follow the existing seam style and run on ci without real ps |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/env/io_execution_env.dart | ⚠️ important ac1 s integration leg is missing — the fixed walk path has zero real process coverage anywhere issue 2276 ac1 https github com istin flutter agent harness issues 2276 demands an integration check on a non setsid host background job sh c trap term sleep 300 wait bash job stop then no live process matches the job s command 1s later this pr s suite is seam only the dev mac cannot run bin ps — honestly disclosed in the description but ci does not close the gap either ci linux has setsid so every default stop takes the owngroup group kill path — the walk at line 563 never runs the only forced walk leg test env io execution env test dart 546 ownprocessgroupoverride false kills a trap less direct child sleep 605 1053 never the reaped leader term trapping reparented grandchild shape this pr fixes so the real ps table parse real reparenting timing and the real kill round re root are never exercised against the bug they were changed for — on any host in any run the seam test pins the call pattern not the walk s behavior over a real table the fake reimplements the observability filter itself ask extend the walk fallback leg or add one beside it with the ac1 shape — ci runnable on linux via the existing ownprocessgroupoverride false e g trap term sleep marker wait behind a stop asserting the marker process is gone 1s and ideally that a walk miss would have been adopted card b rather than answering stopped |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

# PR Diff Truncated

Original size: 30916 characters.
Kept: first 7800 and last 4200 characters.

The full diff is available in the checked-out PR branch. Use `git diff` or CodeGraph for focused source navigation instead of relying only on this file.

```diff
diff --git a/lib/src/env/execution_env.dart b/lib/src/env/execution_env.dart
index c6ec51d0b0..4d7efac1d0 100644
--- a/lib/src/env/execution_env.dart
+++ b/lib/src/env/execution_env.dart
@@ -307,6 +307,7 @@ final class ExecutionError implements Exception {
     this.cause,
     this.stdout = '',
     this.stderr = '',
+    this.survivors = const [],
   });

   /// Backend-independent error code.
@@ -329,6 +330,13 @@ final class ExecutionError implements Exception {
   /// [stdout].
   final String stderr;

+  /// Live processes a killed run left behind on hosts where the tree walk
+  /// is best-effort (issue #2276). Keeping these on the error is essential:
+  /// timeout/cancel results are errors, so putting them only on
+  /// [ShellExecResult] would discard them before the bash tool can adopt
+  /// and report the survivors.
+  final List<ShellSurvivor> survivors;
+
   @override
   String toString() => 'ExecutionError(${code.name}): $message';
 }
@@ -477,9 +485,12 @@ final class ShellExecResult {

   /// Live processes this call left behind, detected at the direct child's
   /// exit (issue #2201). Empty everywhere the platform cannot scan
-  /// (Windows, web, sandboxed shells); a normal-exit-only signal —
-  /// timeout/cancel kills reap the whole tree (gh-1053), so survivors
-  /// there are never reported.
+  /// (Windows, web, sandboxed shells). On stop exits (timeout/cancel) it
+  /// fills only on hosts without group leadership — there the tree kill
+  /// is a best-effort walk whose reparented TERM-trapping grandchildren
+  /// can survive it, and adoption re-tracks them (issue #2276); on
+  /// ownGroup hosts the group kill reaps the whole tree (gh-1053), so
+  /// survivors there are never reported.
   final List<ShellSurvivor> survivors;
 }

@@ -569,8 +580,11 @@ abstract interface class BackgroundShell {
 /// the same survivors the foreground exec path reports through
 /// [ShellExecResult.survivors], surfaced here because a detached job's
 /// completion reaches the registry, not a tool result. Jobs whose shells
-/// cannot scan (or that were stopped/timed out — gh-1053 reaps those
-/// trees) never implement this or return empty.
+/// cannot scan never implement this or return empty; a stopped/timed-out
